cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you build on this software, findings, or ideas, please cite this repository and the exact commit used."
type: software
title: "RBC: Relational Belief Compilation"
authors:
  - family-names: Legotin
    given-names: Artem
version: 0.1.0
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/arlegotin/RBC"
url: "https://github.com/arlegotin/RBC"
abstract: >-
  An exact joint-belief policy executor and replayable returns-case
  experiment. On 500 generated development cases, joint support accepted 168
  decisions versus 158 for independent oracle marginals, while a conventional
  public-text parser matched the joint oracle. The two-percentage-point
  advantage fell below the predeclared continuation gate; learned compilation
  and independent human-written validation were not attempted.
keywords:
  - joint beliefs
  - uncertainty
  - policy execution
  - selective prediction
  - relational reasoning
  - negative results
